<owl:Class rdf:about="#00208">
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="#00206"/>
  <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Food_Insecurity</rdfs:label>
  <core:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Limited or uncertain availability of nutritionally adequate and safe foods or limited or uncertain ability to acquire acceptable foods in safe and socially acceptable ways. (MSH)
 The state of being uncertain about future access to nutritionally adequate and affordable foods. (SNOMEDCT_US)
 Uncertain, limited, or unstable access to food that is adequate in quantity and in nutritional quality; culturally acceptable; safe and acquired in socially acceptable ways. (SNOMEDCT_US)
 An individual's concern about consistent access to sufficient quantities of affordable, nutritious food for an active, healthy life. (NCI)
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C3494174</core:definition>
  <ICD10CM_ID rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Z59.4</ICD10CM_ID>
  <UMLS_CUI rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C3494174</UMLS_CUI>
  <UMLS_Semantic_Type rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Finding</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
</owl:Class>

